atomic_contract_planning.template:
Return strict JSON only with selected_route, slots, route_reason, and confidence. Each slot must contain description, requested_measure (string or null), source_name_hints, authorized_source_doc_ids, locator_hints, expected_answer_type, expected_result_unit (string or null), conditions, depends_on_slot_ids, and visual_policy. Each condition must contain field, operator, value, and unit (string or null). Separate the requested result from conditions: values that constrain the question belong only in conditions and can never be requested_measure or an expected result. Use one to eight answer-free slots. Dependencies may reference only earlier slot IDs. Locator hints must be bounded source locations such as Figure, Table, Appendix, Formula, Equation, Theorem, Page, Section, source passage, or a named equation or matrix. Never answer the question, invent values, or expand or mismatch the supplied source names and IDs. Use only the original question and the authoritative source metadata below; never use or request benchmark answers, gold facts, reference answers, expected values, retrieved answers, or opaque name-to-ID guesses.

Question: {question}
Authorized source names: {authorized_source_names}
Authorized document IDs: {authorized_doc_ids}
Authoritative source mapping: {authorized_source_mapping}
Return the atomic contract JSON object.
